# Prototype Invariants

Read `docs/DECISIONS.md` and `docs/PATTERNS.md` when changing review, handoff, comments, verification, or forms.

- The workflow separates import/data accuracy from AI diagnostics; do not reintroduce redundant findings across phases.
- Phase 2 remains visibly explained and locked until Phase 1 completion requirements are met.
- Document verification is additive and traceable across people. A later reviewer never erases an earlier person's stamp.
- Document comments use the shared annotation criticality model and register in the shared comments tray.
- Form checks use L1, L2, and L3. The first actor at a level becomes the displayed owner; preparer maps to L1, reviewer to L2, manager to L3.
- Review state and notes persist and synchronize across tabs/windows using the established hooks and storage namespaces.
- Handoff uses the large modal. Its AI summary and reviewer notes fill and align to the content width.
- Handoff summaries are concise and structured, and include a heads-up section for unresolved, unchecked, or critical items.
- Reopening diagnostics from a contextual entry point must not unexpectedly hide the user's Summary after first use.
- Preserve existing routes, role switching, diagnostics entry, comments tray, form output views, and document review unless explicitly changed.
- Prototype-specific ports, base paths, repositories, and storage prefixes come from `PROTO_C3_REQUIREMENTS.md`; do not infer them from sibling repos.
